  "description": "a cone of radius 2 and height 4 revolved about z, its apex at (0, 0, 2), less a half-space whose face runs through the apex and the chord y = 1 of the base: the plane meets the cone in two rulings that end on the apex. The section vertex there is the operand's own — the seam ends on the apex and pierces the plane at it — but the apex is a whole line of (u, v) on the cone, held by a degenerate edge that has no curve and is hit by nothing, so that edge is paved at the two `u` the rulings arrive with (ADR-0021), which is where the face's arrangement needs its nodes: without them both rulings reached the one corner of the (u, v) box and read as a tangent contact. The result keeps the apex and the piece of the degenerate edge between the rulings. The tilt is atan(1/4), written out, so the chord is at half the radius and the segment it cuts from the base is 4π/3 − √3 exactly: the solid is the cone over the rest of the disc, a third of the height times that area, its centroid a quarter of the way from the base region's to the apex; the wall kept is two thirds of the cone's, and the cut face the triangle of base 2√3 and height √17",
